  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday night through Saturday)\nIssued at 1208 AM CDT Sun Oct 4 2026\n\nOur pleasant weather continues as northerly flow is seen in the \nlower and middle parts of the atmosphere leading to a continued \ndrying out across our area. This drier air will result in a much \nmore refreshing airmass with cooler mornings and milder afternoons \nalong with much lower humidity. Daily highs stay in the 80s for the \nwhile the morning lows dip down as low as the upper 50s across the \nHill Country and into the low to mid 60s elsewhere. This begins to \nchange by late week as medium range models start to differ on the \nevolution of a possible disturbance located over the southwestern \nGulf thats associated with the the Central American Gyre. For now \nthis is a bit too far out to put any confidence in a particular \nmodel solution. We will continue to keep an eye on this disturbance \nand watch to see how this unfolds and plays out and what impacts if \nany this would bring to our local area. Stay tuned.",
